    arXiv:2104.15129 · arXiv:2108.09187 · arXiv:2110.13541
    QuRA (arXiv:2510.09647) · Quantization Blindspots (arXiv:2512.06243)
    Repairs: EFRAP (CVPR 2024), QVec, FlipGuard, QuantGuard

  Certified poisoning defence, group-and-vote
    Bagging (arXiv:2008.04495)
    Deep Partition Aggregation / Finite Aggregation (arXiv:2202.02628)
    Run-Off Election (arXiv:2302.02300) — the aggregator we use
    Lethal Dose Conjecture (arXiv:2208.03309)
    CBD (arXiv:2310.17498) — model-level certified detection with an FPR bound

  Contributor-denominated certification
    FLCert (arXiv:2210.00584, IEEE TIFS) — owns the client-denominated certificate
    CARVY-FL (arXiv:2608.28992)

  E-values and anytime-valid inference
    Vovk & Wang (arXiv:1912.06116, Ann. Statist. 49(3)) — merging by averaging
    Conformal test martingales (arXiv:2102.10439)
    WATCH (arXiv:2505.04608, ICML 2025) — weighted monitoring and shift diagnosis
    e-detectors (arXiv:2203.03532)

  Quantisation-error verification — stronger than us over the region it covers
    QEBVerif (arXiv:2212.02781)
    ReluDiff / NeuroDiff / VeryDiff (arXiv:2001.03662, 2009.09943, 2410.20207)

  Machine-readable assurance argumentation
    AMLAS lineage (arXiv:2211.04530)
    Evidential Tool Bus (arXiv:2403.01918)
    ScenicProver (arXiv:2511.02164)
    AIRS (arXiv:2511.12668) — the nearest integrated system

  Signed model provenance
    Sigstore model-transparency, in-toto, SLSA — they attest bytes and signer, and
    their own documentation states they do not attest behaviour.

  The limit that bounds every row above
    Planting Undetectable Backdoors in Machine Learning Models
