DELIBERATELY NOT BUNDLED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  BackdoorBench (https://github.com/SCLBD/BackdoorBench)
    CC BY-NC-4.0 — NonCommercial, which is not an open-source licence under the Open
    Source Definition and is a direct obstacle to this project's deployment path. It
    lives in research/, is excluded from the container image and from
    offline-manifest.yaml, and is used only to cross-check our own attack
    implementations. The attacks that ship are ours, written from the original papers.

  Redis
    Left BSD-3-Clause in March 2024; now tri-licensed AGPLv3 / SSPLv1 / RSALv2. We use
    Valkey (BSD-3-Clause, Linux Foundation) instead. A defence assurance instrument
    should not carry a source-available dependency, and the swap is one line.

  torchvision pretrained weights
    `pretrained=True` is simultaneously an air-gap violation (clause 2.2.6) and a
    reference-contamination bug: a backbone trained on the procurement corpus makes the
    poisoned shards part of the reference the detector measures deviation from. Our
    backbone is trained in-house on a declared, disjoint public corpus.
